lass="leftmenu"><a href="/angular-spring-crud-example">CRUD Example</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angular-spring-login-and-logout-example">Login &amp; Logout Example</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angular-spring-search-field-example">Search Field Example</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="accordion-item" style="background-color:var(--sidebar)"><h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading5"><button aria-controls="flush-collapse5" aria-expanded="true" class="accordion-button sidebar-btn" data-bs-target="#flush-collapse5" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button">Interview Questions</button></h2><div aria-labelledby="flush-heading5" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" id="flush-collapse5"><div class="accordion-body"><ul><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-interview-questions">AngularJS Interview</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/javascript-interview-questions">JavaScript Interview</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/jquery-interview-questions">jQuery Interview</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/ember-js-interview-questions">Ember.js Interview</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/neo4j-interview-questions-and-answers">Neo4j Interview</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="accordion-item" style="background-color:var(--sidebar)"><h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading6"><button aria-controls="flush-collapse6" aria-expanded="true" class="accordion-button sidebar-btn" data-bs-target="#flush-collapse6" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button">AngularJS Directives</button></h2><div aria-labelledby="flush-heading6" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" id="flush-collapse6"><div class="accordion-body"><ul><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-app-directive">1) ng-app</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-bind-directive">2) ng-bind</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-bind-html-directive">3) ng-bind-html</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-blur-directive">4) ng-blur</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-bind-template-driective">5) bind-template</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-change-directive">6) ng-change</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-checked-directive">7) ng-checked</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-class-directive">8) ng-class</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-class-even-directive">9) ng-class-even</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-class-odd-directive">10) ng-class-odd</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-click-directive">11) ng-click</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-cloak-directive">12) ng-cloak</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-controller-directive">13) ng-controller</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-copy-directive">14) ng-copy</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-csp-directive">15) ng-csp</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-cut-directive">16) ng-cut</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-dblclick-directive">17) ng-dblclick</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-focus-directive">18) ng-focus</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-hide-directive">19) ng-hide</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-href-directive">20) ng-href</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-if-directive">21) nf-if</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-include-directive">22) ng-include</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-init-directive">23) ng-init</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-jq-directive">24) ng-jq</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-keydown-directive">25) ng-keydown</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-keypress-directive">26) ng-keypress</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-keyup-directive">27) ng-keyup</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-list-directive">28) ng-list</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-open-directive">29) ng-open</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-options-directive">30) ng-options</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-paste-directive">31) ng-paste</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-pluralize-directive">32) ng-pluralize</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-readonly-directive">33) ng-readonly</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-required-directive">34) ng-required</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-selected-directive">35) ng-selected</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-show-directive">36) ng-show</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-src-directive">37) ng-src</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-srcset-directive">38) ng-srcset</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-style-directive">39) ng-style</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-submit-directive">40) ng-submit</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-switch-directive">41) ng-switch</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-transclude-directive">42) ng-transclude</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/angularjs-ng-value-directive">43) ng-value</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-12 col-md-7"><div class="overview"><div id="city"><table><tbody><tr><td><div id="bottomnextup"><a class="next" href="what-is-angularjs">next →</a></div><h1 class="h1">AngularJS Tutorial | Angular Tutorial</h1><div style="font-size:14px;margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:#6f6e6e"><span>10 Mar 2025</span> | <span><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 6 min read</span></div><h2 class="h2">Introduction</h2><p>Angular is an open-source, JavaScript framework which is written in Typescript. Angular is mainly used to develop single-page applications which is maintained by Google.</p><p>With the help of Angular, developers can create robust, scalable, and maintainable web applications. Angular also provides a standard structure for developers so they can work with.</p><p>AngularJS is a known <a href="javascript-tutorial">JavaScript framework</a> that Google created to make web application development and testing easier. It offers a methodical way to create dynamic <a href="spa-authentication-in-mean-stack">single-page applications (SPAs)</a> and many business applications. It is provided the strong capabilities to <a href="html-tutorial">HTML</a> such as modularization, dependency injection, and two-way data binding. AngularJS is frequently utilized in smaller projects and legacy applications with the rise of its replacement, Angular.</p><h2 class="h2">History</h2><p>Angular, originally released as AngularJS in 2010 by Goggle, revolutionized web development with features like two-way data binding and dependency injection. In 2016, the framework underwent a major rewrite to <a href="angular-2">Angular 2</a>, the use of <a href="typescript-tutorial">Typescript</a> and adopting a component based architecture.</p><p>Since then, Angular has persisted to evolve with regular updates, which improve overall performance, modularity and developer t. The framework remains a popular preference for building modern web applications.</p><h2 class="h2">AngularJS Learning Prerequisites</h2><p>It is advantageous to have a strong foundation in the following technologies before beginning to build using AngularJS:</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>HTML &amp; CSS:</strong> Web application structure and styling require a basic mastery of HTML and CSS.</li><li><strong>JavaScript:</strong> Working with AngularJS requires an understanding of JavaScript, especially its ES5 and ES6 features.</li><li><strong>Basic Programming Concepts:</strong> Gaining an understanding of programming basics such as loops, functions, and conditions facilitates the rapid acquisition of AngularJS.</li><li><strong>DOM:</strong> An understanding of the Document Object Model can help you comprehend how AngularJS works with HTML elements.</li><li><strong>AJAX and RESTful Services:</strong> A basic understanding of AJAX and API calls is helpful to manage server-side data transactions.</li></ul><h2 class="h2">AngularJS development Prerequisites</h2><p>The following equipment and software are needed to set up an AngularJS development environment:</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>Web Browser:</strong> Any contemporary web browser, such as Microsoft Edge, Mozilla Firefox, Google Chrome, etc.</li><li><strong>Code Editor:</strong> A text editor such as Atom, Sublime Text, or Visual Studio Code.</li><li><strong>Web Server:</strong> Using a lightweight web server, such as Apache or Node.js, can improve development productivity, although it is not required.</li><li><strong>AngularJS Library:</strong> You can download the most recent version of the AngularJS library locally or include it via a CDN.</li></ul><h2 class="h2">Why do we use Angular?</h2><p>JavaScript is the most commonly used <a href="advantages-and-disadvantages-of-client-side-scripting">client-side scripting language</a>. It is written into HTML documents that enable interactions with web pages in many unique ways.</p><p>It is a popular framework for web development that is used to build single-page applications.</p><p>There are some reasons why we use Angular, such as:</p><h3 class="h3">Data binding</h3><p>Angular allows for two-way data binding between the model and the view. It means that when we make any changes to a component are automatically updated.</p><h3 class="h3">MVC architecture</h3><p>Angular uses the model view controller MVC architecture which is a foundation for data binding and scopes.</p><h3 class="h3">Code consistency</h3><p>Angular uses the CLI tool helps developers establish projects, perform tests, and add new functionality.</p><h3 class="h3">Dependency injection</h3><p>With the help of Angular, users can write modular services and inject them wherever they are needed. It also improves the testability and reusability of the same services.</p><h3 class="h3">Comprehensive</h3><p>Angular is a full-fledged JavaScript framework and it also provide out-of-the-box solutions for server communication with route within your application and more.</p><h3 class="h3">Browser Compatibility</h3><p>It also works on cross-platforms and compatible with multiple browsers. An angular application can typically run on all browsers such as <a href="google-chrome">Chrome</a>, <a href="mozilla-firefox">Firefox</a> and <a href="operating-system">operating systems</a>, such as <a href="windows">Windows</a>, <a href="what-is-macos">macOS</a>, and <a href="linux-tutorial">Linux</a>.</p><h2 class="h2">How to Create an Angular Application</h2><p>There are some steps you need to follow to create an angular application:</p><p><strong>Step 1: Install Angular CLI</strong></p><p>Angular CLI is a tool that is used for scaffolding and manage Angular applications. You need to install it globally with the use of npm:</p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">npm install -g @angular/cli
</textarea></div><p><strong>Step 2: Create a New Angular Project</strong></p><p>Use Angular CLI to create a new Angular project and navigate to the desired directory and run:</p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">ng new my-angular-app
</textarea></div><p><strong>Step 3: Navigate to the Project Directory</strong></p><p>After that, move into the newly created project directory:</p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">cd my-angular-app
</textarea></div><p><strong>Step 4: Serve the Application</strong></p><p>Then, launch the development server to see your app in action:</p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">ng serve
</textarea></div><p><strong>Structure of Folder:</strong></p><img alt="AngularJS Tutorial | Angular Tutorial" src="https://d2jdgazzki9vjm.cloudfront.net/js/angularjs/images/angularjs-tutorial1.png"><p><strong>Dependencies</strong></p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">  "dependencies": {
    "@angular/animations": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/common": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/compiler": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/core": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/forms": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/platform-browser": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/platform-browser-dynamic": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/platform-server": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/router": "^19.1.0",
    "@angular/ssr": "^19.1.7",
    "express": "^4.18.2",
    "rxjs": "~7.8.0",
    "tslib": "^2.3.0",
    "zone.js": "~0.15.0"
  }
</textarea></div><h3 class="h3">Example</h3><p><strong>HTML</strong></p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;MyAngularApp&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;base href="/"&gt;
  &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"&gt;
  &lt;link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="favicon.ico"&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Hello Angular&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;app-root&gt;&lt;/app-root&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</textarea></div><p><strong>JavaScript</strong></p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { RouterOutlet } from '@angular/router';

@Component({
    selector: 'app-root',
    standalone: true,
    imports: [RouterOutlet],
    templateUrl: './app.component.html',
    styleUrl: './app.component.css'
})
export class AppComponent {
    title = 'my-angular-app';
}
</textarea></div><p><strong>Structure of Folder:</strong></p><img alt="AngularJS Tutorial | Angular Tutorial" src="https://d2jdgazzki9vjm.cloudfront.net/js/angularjs/images/angularjs-tutorial2.png"><h2 class="h2">Features of Angular</h2><p>There are some of features of Angular such as:</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>Two-Way Data binding:</strong> Angular provides seamless synchronization between the model and the view which helps the developer for easy management of user inputs.</li><li><strong>Directives:</strong> In Angular, directives allow you to extend HTML with custom behaviour. It also provides built-in directives such as nglf, ngFor, and ngStyle, and you can also create your own custom directives to meet specific requirements.</li><li><strong>Services:</strong> In Angular, services are single instance objects that are used to organize and share code across components. They encapsulate reusable functionality such as data fetching authentication, and business logic.</li><li><strong>Routing:</strong> Angular built-in router allows you to build single page applications with multiple views. It also provides features like nested routes, lazy loading, route guards, and parameterized routes which enables complex navigation scenarios.</li><li><strong>Forms:</strong> In Angular, we have two types of forms: template-driven forms and reactive forms. Template driven forms are bases on directives while reactive forms are model driven and offer more flexibility and control.</li></ul><h2 class="h2">Applications for AngularJS</h2><p>The main purpose of AngularJS is to create dynamic online applications especially SPAs. it is necessary for smooth communication between many components. Among the important use cases are:</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>Applications (SPAs):</strong> AngularJS is frequently used to create SPAs, which allow users to move around the application without having to reload the whole page.</li><li><strong>Enterprise Web Applications:</strong> AngularJS is a popular option for intricate corporate applications because of its well-organized Model-View-Controller (MVC) design.</li><li><strong>PWAs or progressive web applications:</strong> They become lighter, more responsive, and more performant with its support.</li><li><strong>E-commerce Websites:</strong> Because of AngularJS's strong structure and support for dynamic content rendering, many e-commerce websites use it.</li><li><strong>Content Management Systems (CMS):</strong> CMS platforms provide adaptable and effective web-based interfaces by utilizing AngularJS.</li><li><strong>Data-Driven Applications:</strong> AngularJS's two-way data binding is advantageous for applications that require real-time updates, such dashboards, charts, and reporting tools.</li></ul><h2 class="h2">Advantages of Angular</h2><p>There are a lot of JavaScript frameworks for building web applications. So, it is a genuine question, why to use Angular JS.</p><p>The Following are advantages of AngularJS over other JavaScript frameworks:</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>Reusable Components:</strong> By enabling the development of reusable components, the framework enhances the maintainability and reusability of code.</li><li><strong>Customization Directives:</strong> By generating reusable user interface elements, custom directives improve HTML functionality.</li><li><strong>Support for RESTful APIs:</strong> AngularJS is perfect for apps that need to exchange data often since it makes interacting with server-side APIs easier.</li><li><strong>Integrated Testing Support:</strong> It guarantees reliable application development by supporting both unit and end-to-end testing.</li><li><strong>Cross-Browser Compatibility:</strong> All modern web browsers can easily run AngularJS applications.</li></ul><h2 class="h2">Limitations of Angular</h2><p>There are some limitations of angular, such as:</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>Limited SEO Options:</strong> A major drawback of using Angular is the limited SEO options and poor accessibility for search engine crawlers.</li><li><strong>Learning curve:</strong> Angular has a steep learning curve especially for beginners, due to its complex concepts and extensive documentation.</li><li><strong>Performance overhead:</strong> Angular have powerful features that comes with a performance cost and poorly optimized applications may suffer from performance issues.</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> Angular applications tend to have larger file sizes compared to other frameworks which may impact load times especially on mobile devices.</li><li><strong>Migration:</strong> upgrading between major Angular versions can be challenging and time consuming which require significant changes to existing codebases.</li></ul><h2 class="h2">Conclusion</h2><p>In conclusion, Angular is a robust and feature rich framework for building modern web applications. It also has powerful features such as extensive tooling, and strong community support, Angular remains a popular choice for developers which aims to create scalable and maintainable SPAs. It offers immense potential for building dynamic and interactive web experiences.</p><h2 class="h2">Prerequisite</h2><p>Before learning AngularJS, you must have the basic knowledge of JavaScript.</p><h2 class="h2">Audience</h2><p>Our AngularJS tutorial is designed to help beginners and professionals.</p><h2 class="h2">Problem</h2><p>We assure that you will not find any problem in this AngularJS tutorial. But if there is any mistake, please post the problem in contact form.</p><hr/><div class="nexttopicdiv"><span class="nexttopictext">Next Topic</span><span class="nexttopiclink"><a href="what-is-angularjs">What is AngularJS</a></span></div><div id="bottomnext"><a class="next" href="what-is-angularjs" style="float:right">next →</a></div></img></img></td></tr></tbody></table></div><br/></div><div class="related-posts-container"><h2 class="h3">Related Posts</h2><ul class="related-posts-list"><li><a class="related-post-item" href="angularjs-validation"><h3 class="h3">AngularJS Validation</h3><p class="related-post-content">AngularJS Form Validation AngularJS provides client-side form validation. It checks the state of the form and input fields (input, textarea, select), and lets you notify the user about the current state. It also holds the information about whether the input fields have been touched, or modified, or not. Following...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 6 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3-18.2-.3z"></path></svg></span></p></a></li><li><a class="related-post-item" href="angularjs-mvc-architecture"><h3 class="h3">AngularJS MVC</h3><p class="related-post-content">Architecture MVC stands for Model View Controller. It is a software design pattern for developing web applications. It is very popular because it isolates the application logic from the user interface layer and supports the separation of concerns. AngularJS, a popular JavaScript framework created by Google,...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 5 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3-18.2-.3z"></path></s